        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If there is a need to \"re-send the invoice to the customer\", then proceed with continuing the process.",
        "If the option is to \"post the invoice\", then also continue the process.",
        "Alternatively, if the decision is to \"block the invoice\", then again continue the process.",
        "Once these steps are completed, park the invoice."
      ],
      "justification": "The three conditional branches all explicitly direct the flow to continue, effectively converging on the next major step. The model simplifies this structural branching into a direct transition to parking, which preserves the end-to-end behavior without altering outcomes or ordering."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After the invoice has been handled, the process comes to an end."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures both the explicit terminal action and the structural end node describing process completion."
    }
